WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.400
Shlomi: Moshe, I miss you.

2
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:07.300
I know you're looking at all of us from
over there. Rest in peace.

3
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:09.350
Galia: Love you, Dod Moshe.

4
00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:14.950
Keep doing where you are, what you have
meant, what you managed to do here on
earth.

5
00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:21.290
Ruthie (in Hebrew): My dear uncle, I will
never forget you.

6
00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:28.790
Thank you for what you were in my life.
And may you rest in peace forever and
ever. Amen.

7
00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:31.780
Steve: Alav hashalom.

8
00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:34.480
Peace be upon him.

9
00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:39.910
Debbie: Moshe, you are a special gift and
truly exceptional.

10
00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:41.860
You will be missed.

11
00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:46.410
Micah: I was just saying thank you to Dod
Moshe. Todah, Dod Moshe.

12
00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:53.370
Tali: Moshe, I love you. May your life and
legacy and energy continue to live on.

13
00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:59.170
And I'm always thinking of you in my
heart. Love you.

14
00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:02.470
Aimee: Uncle Moshe, you will live in our
hearts forever.

15
00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:08.560
David Norsoph: Well, Moshe, keep smiling,
and may the pool of women be even more
plentiful in heaven than on earth.

16
00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:12.010
Spoiler alert. That's not really how it
works, okay?

17
00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:13.610
You never know.

18
00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:16.580
David Gudai: Yitgadal v'yitkadash.

19
00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:21.480
Daniel: Well, the only appropriate thing
for me is just to sing, really.

20
00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:27.080
[Singing] Moshe-le, I love you so much,
Mo.

21
00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:31.780
Love you. Miss you. Thank you for having
an amazing impact on my life.

22
00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:38.680
And I will continue to share your spirit
and your happiness with the world. Thank
you, Moshe.

23
00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:42.060
Michael: L'ilui nishmat Moshe ben Sivia.

24
00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:48.960
[Blessing in Hebrew] Amen.

25
00:01:49.080 --> 00:02:00.420
[Michael recites El Malei Rachamim for
Moshe ben Sivia]

26
00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:01.720
Amen.

27
00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:07.920
Jeremy: Moshe, may your memory and legacy
continue to live on throughout all of us
and all generations to come.

28
00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:11.740
Mor: [a blessing, spoken quietly]

29
00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:20.040
Jonathan: We will continue to honor Moshe
for as long as we live, and to remember
him.

30
00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:23.740
And he is going to continue to be with us
for as long as we live.

31
00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:27.240
To Moshe Yeffet. We love you.
